    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by its ending calendar year \u2014 e.g. October 2026 \u2192 **FY27**).\n\n**New shared helper** \u2014 `OwnerFiscalYear.java` is the single source of truth, used by all three date-derived values so they can't drift:\n- `fiscalYear(date)` \u2192 year+1 from July onward, else the year.\n- `label(...)` \u2192 the `FY<YY>` string.\n- `elapsedFiscalYears(from, to)` \u2192 whole 1-July boundaries crossed, never negative.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`fiscalYear` read field** (new) \u2014 added to the `OwnerDto` schema in `openapi.yml` (`readOnly`, `FY<YY>`), derived at read time in `OwnerMapper` via a `@Named(\"fiscalYear\")` method from the stored business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`. This satisfies the `coreReturnsFiscalYear` test.\n2. **Membership identifier** \u2014 `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` now derives the `-M<YY>` segment from the fiscal year instead of the raw registration-date year (behaviour change: a current registration now yields `-M27`, visible in the audit log).\n3. **Tenure** \u2014 `AssignOwnerMembershipLevel` now counts tenure in elapsed fiscal years (threshold: more than 1) instead of 365-day windows; a just-created owner still has zero tenure and earns no tenure points.\n4. Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to match.\n\nNote on convention: the task said `FY<YY>` with the year starting 1 July but didn't pin whether to label by the start or end year. I used the standard Australian convention (named by the ending year, matching the NSW/VIC/QLD context already in the code). No test pins the exact value, so if you'd prefer start-year labeling (`FY26` for an Oct-2026 registration) it's a one-line change in `OwnerFiscalYear.fiscalYear`.",
