    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- **Right unit / single source of truth.** The new `OwnerFiscalYear` class mirrors the established helper pattern exactly \u2014 `OwnerAgeBand`, `OwnerCustomerCode`, and `BusinessDays` are all `final` classes with private constructors, static methods, a \"single source of truth\" doc, and both `Owner`-taking and `LocalDate`-taking overloads. `OwnerFiscalYear` adopts the same shape. Putting the fiscal-year arithmetic in one place is the correct call given three consumers (mapper, membership number, membership level) that must agree.\n\n- **No duplication.** Both `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` and `AssignOwnerMembershipLevel` now delegate to `OwnerFiscalYear` instead of carrying their own `getYear() % 100` / `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between` logic. The now-unused `ChronoUnit` import is correctly dropped. `tenureFiscalYears` stays a small private helper in the level step (keeping the null/registration-date handling local) while the shared boundary math lives in `OwnerFiscalYear.elapsedFiscalYears` \u2014 a reasonable split, not a leftover.\n\n- **Mapper wiring is consistent.** The `@Named(\"fiscalYear\")` default delegating to `OwnerFiscalYear.label(owner)` matches the existing `identityKey`/`checkDigit`/`ageBand` delegations line-for-line, including the null-handling-in-the-helper convention.\n\n- **Nothing is becoming a catch-all.** `OwnerFiscalYear` has a single cohesive responsibility; the Assign steps shrank rather than grew.\n\n- Docs/OpenAPI and the constant rename (`TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS` \u2192 `TENURE_THRESHOLD_FISCAL_YEARS`) are kept in step with the behaviour, so a maintainer reading either the code or the schema gets a consistent story.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this a natural extension of the existing `Owner<Derived>` helper family.",
